<section xml:id="diffeq-notes-7-1" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <title> Gaussian Elimination </title>

    <objectives>
        <introduction>
            <p>
                Students will be able to...
            </p>
        </introduction>
        <ol>
            <li><p> Multiply matrices. </p></li>
            <li><p> Solve systems of equations through Gaussian Elimination. </p></li>
        </ol>
    </objectives>

    <theorem xml:id="thm-row-ops">
        <statement>
            <p>
                The following row operations can be conducted without changing the value of a matrix.
                <ol>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            Rearranging
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            Scalar multiplication.
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            Linear combination.
                        </p>
                    </li>
                </ol>
            </p>
        </statement>
    </theorem>
    

    <exercise>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Use Gaussian Elimination to solve <md> \begin{cases} 5x - 2y = -6; \\ -x + 5y = 15. \end{cases} </md> 
            </p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>

    <theorem xml:id="thm-mtx-mult">
        <statement>
            <p>
                Suppose <m>A,B</m> are both <m>n \times n</m> matrices. Their product <m>AB</m> is determined elementwise by <md> (AB)_{ij} = \bf{a}_i^T \cdot \bf{b}_j </md>
            </p>
        </statement>
    </theorem>
    

    
</section>
